last of all how can I find out what life  is like as a student at Oxford or  Cambridge this is arguably the most  important question of all I mean how can  you be expected to apply to university  and not know what the life hair is like  fortunately though there are lots of  great resources available online to  answer this question firstly for both  universities each College has its own  website and associated social media  accounts as do some departments these  give an excellent flavor of what student  life is like however recently there has  been a movement to create more  student-led initiatives which give an  honest boots-on-the-ground perspective  some of these projects are under a semi  official guide so for example the some  Peter's College YouTube channel is under  the college's name but is run by  students while other projects are  completely run and curated by students  both the official and unofficial  projects have their own advantages and I  highly recommend that you check out both  for a truly rounded picture of what life  Oxbridge is like and for each University  there are a few projects that deserve  special mention for Cambridge there's  fantastic YouTube channel run by Jake  right a recent Computer Sciences  graduate from Queens College who created  vlogs for his entire degree taking you  with him free lectures problem sheets  bops and many many trips to Wetherspoons  it's a fantastic and well produced  account of life as a Cambridge student I  highly recommend it in addition to this  project on Twitter there is also the  hashtag can tweet project where users at  Cambridge will use the hashtag Cam tweet  in tweets about their daily lives so the  search feed for the hashtag becomes an  interesting cross section across the  whole university going across courses  colleges and years if you have Twitter  than you can follow individual accounts  and those accounts are always very happy  to answer applicants questions in Oxford  there is the sister project hashtag ox  tweet which was the brainchild of  youtuber Jamie miles and instantly  inspired the Cambridge project jamie has  his own fu channel where he's made  several videos talking you through the  admissions process and has also made  several videos about his college and his  degree jamie is also the founder along  with it was truly of the ox blog project  Oxford started in my final year where I  started making weekly videos about my  student life and in the second term I  was joined by Jamie and after I  graduated we both set up the ox blog  channel where a team of five students  from across the university make vlogs  about their lives and they cover  different colleges subjects and year  projects now in its third year and is  still going strong making videos about  every aspect of student life from worked  socializing and everything in between  those are all the questions I hope that  this video has been useful to you and  alleviated at least some of your fears  but before I go I want to emphasize  something I said earlier your background  does not determine how likely it is that  you're going to get into Oxford or  Cambridge the only thing that they care  about is your academic ability and  potential and don't let anybody tell you  otherwise because it's simply not true  people believe in awful lot of myths and  misconceptions about Oxford but this is  the most persistent and it's by far the  most damaging don't be put up lying  because you think that you're not going  to get in because of who you were born  to or where you were born it really  doesn't matter check out all the  websites in the description for more  information and if you can't find the  answer to your question there then  remember that you can contact with  colleges and departments directly about  access issues and if you have a question  to me then you can also leave that down  in the comments below and if I can I'll  try and reply with an answer thanks for  watching if you found this usefu